  note   = {The only line this gate printed on the common path reported the absence of a claim,
            and it fired on 29 of 30 commits. Deleting it was the wrong fix: it is the sole
            stdout on that path, so a checker that ran would be byte-identical to one that did
            not. Meanwhile the corpus self-check ran on every commit and said nothing when it
            passed. The pass line now carries the rule count and the self-check's verdict, and
            that figure moves --- 26 distinct counts across 37 commits touching the corpus, so
            reporting it is not renaming furniture. A first version asserted resolution
            unconditionally and was measured contradicting itself, printing a dangling reference
            on stderr while claiming on stdout that everything resolved; the claim is now
            conditional on the verdict it describes.},
  check  = {pytest hooks/tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_citation_gate_reports_a_figure_that_moves},
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-the-shell-gate-says-what-it-checked,
