  note   = {Measured by running the shell gate on a clean file: zero bytes of output and exit 0.
            shellcheck says nothing when it finds nothing and the script ends in exec, so the
            pass path emitted literally nothing --- the shape this repository refuses in every
            other gate, sitting in the gate that checks the shell those refusals are written in.
            The staged-file count is the figure and it moves, because targets arrive from bazel's
            location expansion and a glob that stopped matching would stage fewer files while
            still exiting 0 silently; the script's own comment records that a find-based version
            once returned nothing. The line is emitted before the exec, since after it this shell
            does not exist and a line written below would never run. Three arms measured: a clean
