            symbol was carried unmeasured throughout. Measured: it probes one interpreter and
            prints an unqualified verdict about the repository, and the word collapses three
            states --- paperkit is broken, it is not installed here, and the interpreter is
            absent --- which have three different owners. The verdict was right and the account
            was missing, which is the harder shape, because a blocker that cannot say which state
            it found cannot be acted on. A dry-run resolve of the local checkout finishes in
            milliseconds and would install one package, so paperkit is neither broken nor
            missing; nothing here installs it, and the declaration says it is a published package
            rather than a path, which is an operator decision this arm does not settle. The probe
            now carries a control, because through a discarded stderr a failing import and a
            missing interpreter are byte-identical. All four branches driven on real inputs,
            including paperkit installed into a throwaway venv reading importable.},
  check  = {pytest hooks/tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_paperkit_arm_names_a_cause_and_carries_a_control},
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-the-census-arm-can-tell-a-failed-read-from-an-empty-one,
  title  = {The poll discards the one field that separates a broken read from an empty one},
  author = {Mike Mol},
  year   = {2026},
  section = {bar-fires},
  note   = {The census block guards whether its reader is executable and names that absence
            honestly, then makes every subsequent call with stderr discarded and only stdout
            read. A reader that runs and fails returns nothing, which is byte-identical to a file
            that legitimately has no such table. Measured against the real reader, the states are
            separable by exit status: a real census reads five lines at rc 0, a markdown file
            with no tables reads one line at rc 0, an undecodable file gives zero lines at rc 1,
            and a missing path zero lines at rc 2. The honest empty carries rc 0, so the
            discriminator existed and was being thrown away. This poll selects every later tick's
            work, so a census whose reader failed would report zero of zero parties listed --- a
            clean-looking line about the census rather than about the read. One guard runs before
            the first interpreted read rather than at ten call sites, and three arms confirm a
            real census still reads its roster, an undecodable file names the failed read, and a
            genuinely empty census reports no signature.},
  check  = {pytest hooks/tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_census_arm_can_tell_a_failed_read_from_an_empty_one},
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-the-island-arm-says-the-dependency-was-inverted,
