  section = {bar-fires},
  note   = {Two ticks running the ceiling caught a new arm and that was recorded as the ceiling
            earning itself. Measured against every arm added since it shipped, ten of eleven were
            resolvable as written and the two it caught were caught in draft, before commit --- so
            the ceiling was not under pressure and the story being told about it was wrong. The
            twenty-three are a fixed inheritance, almost all from the founding commit, and a
            ceiling over a population that neither grows nor shrinks reports the same number every
            run. A bounded evaluator reaching only a constant divided by string literals resolves
            five of them, one more than the hand-count predicted, because an arm classified by eye
            also uses that form: the ceiling is the instrument's figure and never the reader's,
            which is the defect three consecutive ticks were spent repairing. The former value is
            kept so the direction is assertable, and the arm requires the evaluator to exist so
            the fall cannot come from editing a number.},
